        new(
            "researchy-np001-v22-roadmap",
            "V2.2 Roadmap: Measurement, Baryon Asymmetry, Neutrinos, and the CMB Lead the Next Targets",
            "ResearchY Milestone · NP_001 (V2.2 New Physics Roadmap)",
            "With the V2.1 origin program complete, the V2.2 roadmap ranks the physics still unexplained. Top priority: the measurement origin (enabled by the derived measurement basis and state identity), then baryon asymmetry, the neutrino hierarchy, and the full CMB spectrum. Each target lists its expected payoff, required derivations, and possible predictions.",
            "NP_001 produces the V2.2 New Physics Roadmap: physics not explained in V2.0/V2.1 that can now be investigated with the derived origin chain. Candidate topics were baselined against canonical coverage: antimatter/baryon asymmetry (CP derived QG166, asymmetry mechanism OPEN), dark matter (deficit effect derived QG195/206, particle reading OPEN), dark energy/Λ (derived QG230/234, coincidence OPEN), neutrinos (masses QG172/Majorana QG179 derived, ordering OPEN, P2 0νββ pre-registered), hierarchy problems (fermion hierarchy derived, v/m_e irreducible D_044), measurement (basis = two-quadrature reconstruction D_037, collapse QG73 OPEN), information structure (I = KL(ρ‖uniform) QG228 + state identity D_039), cosmological observables (n_s QG237, acoustic peaks QG238, full CMB spectrum OPEN). RANKED by novelty × testability × V2.1-dependence. TOP-10 TARGETS: T1 measurement origin (highest V2.1 dependence — the two-quadrature basis D_037 + state identity D_039 + collapse QG73 → a derived measurement formalism, Born rule as reconstruction fidelity, predictions on measurement-disturbance); T2 information-encoded measurement (unify QG228 + D_039, measurement-as-information, measurement entropy from the octave record); T3 baryon asymmetry (highest novelty — CP phase δ = asin(r) QG166 driving matter–antimatter asymmetry through the complex-state phase D_036; prediction η_B); T4 neutrino mass hierarchy (masses + Majorana derived, ordering open, P2 m_ββ = 2.02 meV sharpened for nEXO/LEGEND-1000); T5 CMB anisotropy spectrum (extend n_s + peaks to the full angular spectrum via the octave rungs); T6 dark-matter particle status (deficit dust as field vs particle, mass scale from Ωm − Ωbaryonic); T7 two-anchor ratio v/m_e (test reducibility of the D_044 boundary with the new tools — a derived relation would predict m_e from v); T8 Λ coincidence (Λ ∝ 1/R² already structural; quantify the present-epoch specialness, predict ΩΛ(t)); T9 collapse/observer (collapse as Difference-readout, observer as reconstructor, no-cloning from the two-quadrature basis); T10 cosmological initial conditions (extend the uniform critical state QG227 to perturbations, sharpen n_s). PRIORITY SEQUENCE: T1/T2 (measurement/information) → T3 (baryon asymmetry) → T4 (neutrinos) → T5 (CMB) → T6–T10. CONSTRAINTS: no new primitives; canonical AT unchanged; all targets respect the five-item irreducible boundary set (R_001). Each target requires its own audit + xUnit suite when taken up.",
            "For non-experts: with the V2.1 program complete — every 'where does this come from?' answered or reduced to five starting points — this roadmap asks what to tackle next. The top priority is measurement itself: the theory has already derived what a measurement basis is, so understanding the act of measurement is the natural next step. Then come the big open questions: why is there more matter than antimatter, the neutrino mass ordering, and the full cosmic microwave background map. Each entry lists what we expect to learn, what must be derived to get there, and what new testable prediction would follow.",
